# Call-site ledger of Sublist3r at 3f5fc6da0142540c56e97c98f9925bb7d0855fb5.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# Ground truth from reading only: the project has no tests, so there is no
# trace. Analysed: sublist3r.py (module sublist3r) and subbrute/ (modules
# subbrute and subbrute.subbrute). Supported: Python 2.7 and Python 3
# (setup.py >=2.7 and README; 3.4 recommended, no ceiling), on Linux and
# on Windows (the README documents the
# installation on Windows). The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in
# macro-benchmark/README.md; Sublist3r.md shows how this ledger applies them
# and records each judgement.
#
# Outside callees of code that runs on both Python versions have their
# Python 3 names: urlparse.urlparse and urllib.unquote of Python 2 are
# urllib.parse.urlparse and urllib.parse.unquote. On Windows,
# subbrute.py:33-36 rebinds multiprocessing.Process to threading.Thread
# when sublist3r imports subbrute, so the process classes are thread classes
# there: each Process call also has its threading.Thread name.
# No default rejections: no candidate has 50 or more sites.

